***************************** T A L Y S **************************4843 1451  183
                                                                  4843 1451  184
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   4843 1451  185
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      4843 1451  186
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    4843 1451  187
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     4843 1451  188
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  4843 1451  189
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        4843 1451  190
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    4843 1451  191
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         4843 1451  192
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      4843 1451  193
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    4843 1451  194
stored in this data file:                                         4843 1451  195
                                                                  4843 1451  196
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   4843 1451  197
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     4843 1451  198
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 4843 1451  199
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   4843 1451  200
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                4843 1451  201
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   4843 1451  202
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    4843 1451  203
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        4843 1451  204
- Recoil data                                                     4843 1451  205
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           4843 1451  206
- Total particle energy spectra                                   4843 1451  207
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      4843 1451  208
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        4843 1451  209
- Residual production cross sections                              4843 1451  210
                                                                  4843 1451  211
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            4843 1451  212
parameterization we refer to [kon19]. If for this specific        4843 1451  213
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   4843 1451  214
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                4843 1451  215
                                                                  4843 1451  216
